  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1101 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nBy Friday, Middle TN will find itself fixed on the eastern fringes\nof an expanding area of high pressure aloft. A shortwave will\nripple through Friday into Saturday that will bring our next bout\nof active weather. Deep gulf moisture will make a return as PWATs\nabove 2\" advect into the area. This will set the stage for bouts\nof heavy rainfall possible Friday evening into Saturday. Severe\nweather does not appear likely at this time as instability values\non the whole are insufficient and profiles are very saturated. The\nbiggest thing we will be looking out for will be the potential for\nlocalized flash flooding, especially given antecedent conditons.\nThe probability of receiving 1\" or more is low to medium, ranging\nfrom ~30% near Nashville to 45-50% along the TN/AL state line. \nActivity will wind down Saturday evening and we will fall back \ninto the hot and muggy pattern we are all too familiar with as we \nmove into next week. The ever-expanding high aloft will continue \nits push over the mid-state, yielding daily low rain chances (20%\nor less) and cranking the heat back up. Highs will be back in the\nmid to upper 90s by Monday and will remain elevated through the \nweek.",
